### 1.2 Determining the Next Version (`V2`–`V5`)

| Bump | Trigger Criteria (Conventional Commits Since Last Tag) | Workspace Example |
|---|---|---|
| **`PATCH`** | `fix(...)`, `perf(...)`, security patches; zero new features and zero contract breaks | {{patch_example}} |
| **`MINOR`** | At least one `feat(...)` backward-compatible feature, additive API/schema change, or deprecation (`PATCH` resets to `0`) | {{minor_example}} |
| **`MAJOR`** | Any `type(...)!` or `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer breaking a `V1` contract, or an approved business-driven major release (`D-NN`) | {{major_example}} |

- **Single Source of Truth (`V6`)**: Version files (`{{version_files}}`) are synchronized via `{{version_sync_cmd}}`.
- **Human decision (`V4`)**: The agent inspects `git log <last-tag>..HEAD`, lists the commits and contract impact, and **proposes** the next version; **{{release_approver}} decides and approves the version**.

