## 2. Production Release Runbook & Integrity Checks (`M6`, `R1`–`R2`)

> **Mandatory Rule `M6`**: The agent **prepares** the checklist and exact commands below after verifying readiness, and **never executes** the merge into `{{production_branch}}`, the version tag, or the production deployment without explicit human execution/approval.

1. **Cut & verify Release Candidate (`{{release_pattern}}`)**:
   - Branch `release/X.Y.Z` from `{{integration_branch}}`, run `{{version_sync_cmd}}`, and run the full test/verification suite on STG. Only `fix/*` branches may target `release/X.Y.Z` (and must also merge back to `{{integration_branch}}`).
2. **Check `R1` — Every Production Hotfix Is Included**:
   ```sh
   git fetch origin --prune
   git log --oneline origin/release/X.Y.Z..origin/{{production_branch}}
   ```
   *(Must be empty — `0` unmerged commits on `{{production_branch}}`.)*
3. **Merge `release/X.Y.Z` into `{{production_branch}}` (`--no-ff`, user-approved/executed)**:
   ```sh
   git switch {{production_branch}}
   git merge --no-ff origin/release/X.Y.Z -m "Release vX.Y.Z"
   ```
4. **Check `R2` — Exact Tree Identity Between Tested Release and `{{production_branch}}`**:
   ```sh
   git diff origin/release/X.Y.Z HEAD
   ```
   *(Must be empty — `0` diff lines.)*
5. **Create Annotated Tag & Atomic Push (user-approved/executed)**:
   ```sh
   git tag -a vX.Y.Z -m "{{project_name}} vX.Y.Z"
   git push --atomic origin {{production_branch}} refs/tags/vX.Y.Z
   ```
   *(Never run `git push --tags` or `git push --all`.)*
6. **Back-Merge & Cleanup**: Merge `{{production_branch}}` back into `{{integration_branch}}` and delete `release/X.Y.Z` after user confirmation.

