## 3. Deterministic CLI Verification Gates (`PASS` / `FAIL`)

All automated checks report strictly **`PASS`** or **`FAIL`** (`shared_contracts/flags_and_statuses.md`; `NOT_RUN`, `BLOCKED`, and `UNVERIFIED` never count as `PASS`):

| Gate | Command | `PASS` Criterion | `FAIL` Action |
|---|---|---|---|
| **G1 — Protected Branch Guard (`M2`)** | `git branch --show-current` | Current branch is not in `{{protected_branches}}` | Switch to the `D-NN` work branch before editing or committing |
| **G2 — Base Ancestry Check (`G1`)** | `git merge-base --is-ancestor origin/<base> HEAD` | Exit `0` | Rebase personal branch onto `origin/<base>` or alert user if wrong base |
| **G3 — Staged Diff Hygiene (`M4`, `M7`)** | `git diff --cached --check && git status --short` | Exit `0`, zero secrets, only task-scoped files staged | Unstage unrelated files (`git restore --staged <path>`) and fix whitespace |
| **G4 — Commit Traceability Gate (`G3`, `M10`)** | `{{commit_check_cmd}}` | Every commit cites `<SUB-TICKET>`, `<PARENT-TICKET> + [PHASE-NN]`, or `(phase-NN)` | Amend/reword personal unpushed commit to restore full ticket/phase traceability |
| **G5 — Release Integrity (`R1` + `R2`)** | `git log origin/release/X.Y.Z..origin/{{production_branch}}` | Empty output (`0` missing hotfixes) | Merge missing hotfix into `release/X.Y.Z` and re-verify on STG |

