## 4. Code Review Severity Rubric (`BLOCKER` / `MAJOR` / `MINOR`)

Reviewer findings on Git workflow and branch hygiene use the unified 3-tier scale from `shared_contracts/flags_and_statuses.md`:

| Severity | Git Workflow Finding Criteria |
|---|---|
| **`BLOCKER`** | • Direct commit or push to a protected branch (`{{protected_branches}}`, `M2`) or unauthorized merge/tag on `{{production_branch}}` (`M6`).<br>• Branch cut from the wrong base (`M1`/`G1`), pulling unverified `{{integration_branch}}` commits into a `{{release_pattern}}` fix or `hotfix/*`.<br>• Secret, token, or `.env` credential staged or committed in branch history (`M7`).<br>• Production hotfix not propagated to active `{{release_pattern}}` and `{{integration_branch}}` (`G5`), or `R1`/`R2` release integrity check failing.<br>• Breaking contract change (`V1`) omitting `!` / `BREAKING CHANGE:` and `D-NN` approval. |
| **`MAJOR`** | • Arbitrary WIP commits (`wip`, `update`, `temp`, `fix bug`) created mid-phase before verification gates pass (`M10`).<br>• Commit subject missing required **Sub-Ticket ID** (`<SUB-TICKET>`) or **Accepted Phase (`PHASE-NN`)** traceability (`G3`).<br>• Branch name violates `<type>/<PARENT-TICKET>-<short-description>` pattern or uses developer personal names (`G2`).<br>• Unrelated files or untracked artifacts staged via `git add .` (`M4`).<br>• Version files (`{{version_files}}`) out of sync with `{{version_sync_cmd}}` (`V6`). |
| **`MINOR`** | • Commit summary exceeds 72 characters or uses past tense instead of imperative mood.<br>• Minor formatting omission in PR description when `D-NN` and commit traceability are otherwise complete. |

